{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on this day.</b> That is to say, 'And it came to pass when a particular day arrived' — a day of merrymaking, a day of their festival, when they all went to the house of idolatry. She said: 'I have no day as fitting as this one to seduce Joseph.' She said to them: 'I am ill and cannot go' (Tanchuma)." "<b>To do his work.</b> Rav and Shmuel — one said: his actual work; and one said: to do his needs with her — but the image of his father's likeness appeared to him, etc., as is found in tractate Sotah (37a)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:45.226625402Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}